<h2 id="13-resultado-iii-2701-el-espejo-palíndromo-y-los-modelos-nul">13. Result III — 2701, the mirror-palindrome, and the null models</h2>
<p>Properties of Genesis 1:1: 2701 = 37×73; 73rd triangular; 2701 + 1072 = 3773 (palindrome).</p>
<p><strong>Selectivity test.</strong> Does the mirror distinguish Genesis from arbitrary text? 30 660 null verses were generated (20× Genesis, n = 1533), with (a) order-1 Markov over the letters of Genesis itself and (b) iid uniform, both with the real <strong>length distribution</strong>. Deterministic PRNG (mulberry32, seed 20260807) for exact reproducibility:</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>property</th><th>Genesis (n=1533)</th><th>Markov ord-1</th><th>uniform iid</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>G + rev(G) = palindrome</td><td><strong>39.3 %</strong> (603)</td><td>38.8 % (11 883)</td><td>38.0 % (11 657)</td></tr><tr><td>G divisible by 37</td><td>3.13 % (48)</td><td>2.80 % (858)</td><td>2.79 % (855)</td></tr><tr><td>G triangular</td><td>1.57 % (24)</td><td>1.20 % (368)</td><td>1.15 % (352)</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>Mirror ratio Genesis/Markov = <strong>1.01×</strong>; Genesis/uniform = 1.03×. <strong>It does not discriminate</strong>: ~4 of every 10 arbitrary Hebrew verses of comparable length already fulfill it, by the arithmetic of digit-reversal sum. Divisibility by 37 shows a weak excess (~1.12×) and triangularity a moderate excess (~1.31×); with n = 1533 neither is conclusive, and both are independent of the mirror.</p>
<h3 id="13-1-nulo-a-nivel-palabra-es-el-palíndromo-espejo-un-checksu">13.1 Word-level null (is the mirror-palindrome a checksum?)</h3>
<p>The "checksum by palindrome" hypothesis (§6.2, §9.5) requires the mirror-palindrome to be <strong>rare</strong>. It is not. Direct test over the Strong lexicon (6045 roots) and the 12 <em>mazzalot</em> (<code>calc_mazzalot.mjs</code>):</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>set</th><th>mirror-palindrome</th><th>rate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Strong lexicon (6045 roots)</td><td>2895</td><td><strong>47.9 %</strong></td></tr><tr><td>12 mazzalot</td><td>7/12</td><td><strong>58 %</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Genesis (verses, n=1533)</td><td>603</td><td>39.3 %</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>By number of digits of the gematria: 1 digit 5.1 %, 2 digits 54.6 %, 3 digits 45.8 %, 4 digits 84.7 %. The rate grows with length because more digit pairs can sum ≤ 9 without carry.</p>
<p><strong>Implication:</strong> ~1 of every 2 arbitrary Hebrew words is a mirror-palindrome. That <em>Egel</em>→404, <em>Ayil</em>→55, <em>Shor</em>→1111 are so is not, by itself, evidence of design: it is what is expected from decimal arithmetic. The mirror <strong>cannot function as a checksum</strong> because it does not discriminate "marked" text from arbitrary text. What is specific to those words are the <strong>sums with astronomical value</strong> (Egel+Ayil = 144; Shor = 2×sum(1..22)) —real arithmetic, but whose attribution to authorial intention requires a null of "numbers with meaning" that is not defined here (multiple-comparisons problem).</p>
<h3 id="13-2-nivel-frase-y-el-palíndromo-como-criterio-de-validez">13.2 Phrase level and the palindrome as a validity criterion</h3>
<p>Two methodological objections require going beyond the word level: (i) the real units of the text are <strong>phrases, verses, and large numbers</strong>, not isolated words; (ii) the hypothesis that the mirror-palindrome is <strong>the method to distinguish which readings of the sky are valid and which are not</strong> (discarding thousands of combinations), not a <em>checksum</em>.</p>
<p><strong>(i) Phrase level.</strong> Computed over the 1533 verses of Genesis (<code>calc_phrase.mjs</code>), broken down by digits of the verse gematria:</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>level</th><th>unit</th><th>mirror-palindrome</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>word</td><td>6045 roots (lexicon)</td><td>47.9 %</td></tr><tr><td><strong>phrase</strong></td><td>verses of Genesis (n=1533)</td><td><strong>39.3 %</strong></td></tr><tr><td>large phrase</td><td>verses with gematria ≥ 1000 (n=1503)</td><td>39.6 %</td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>The phrase is <strong>more selective</strong> than the word (39.3 % vs 47.9 %): the objection is correct in direction. But the rarefaction stops there —long verses (gematria ≥ 1000, already 4 digits) do not palindrome less than the total (39.6 % vs 39.3 %)—, and the rate remains indistinguishable from the Markov null (38.8 %, §13). The magnitude of the number, by itself, does not make the mirror rare.</p>
<p><strong>(ii) The palindrome as a selector of readings.</strong> Direct test: the "phrase of the sky" at a date = the simple letters of the 10 bodies, ordered; its gematria + mirror. Comparing Genesis-legible (valid) vs non-legible (invalid) days over 2024–2030:</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>day class</th><th>mirror-palindrome</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Genesis-legible (n=293)</td><td><strong>30.7 %</strong></td></tr><tr><td>Genesis-non-legible (n=2262)</td><td><strong>32.4 %</strong></td></tr></tbody></table>
<p>If the palindrome were the validity criterion, the legible ones would palindrome <em>more</em>. They palindrome <em>less</em> (30.7 % < 32.4 %). <strong>The palindrome does not select the valid readings.</strong> What does select them —and discards 88.5 % of dates (§10)— is the <strong>positional</strong> rule <em>S</em> ⊆ <em>O</em>. The mirror and set membership are independent criteria; the second operates, the first does not separate.</p>
<blockquote><strong>Synthesis.</strong> The mirror-palindrome is real in specific cases (2701→3773, Egel→404) and the phrase is more selective than the word (39 % vs 48 %), but it does not suffice to be either a <em>checksum</em> or a <em>criterion of reading validity</em>: it does not distinguish from a Markov null, it does not rarefy with magnitude, and it does not separate legible from invalid days. The operational discard of the <em>Reader of the Sky</em> is <strong>positional</strong> (<em>S</em> ⊆ <em>O</em>), not arithmetic. What is attested and, for the 72 verses, demonstrated, is the <strong>intentional letter engineering</strong> as a practice (§6.3) —a historical fact, distinct from the statistical selectivity of the mirror.</blockquote>
<h3 id="13-3-el-núcleo-original-génesis-1-donde-el-exceso-sí-aparece">13.3 The original nucleus (Genesis 1): where the excess does appear</h3>
<p>A methodological objection to the null of §13 is the <strong>unit</strong>: measuring isolated verses or loose letters can <strong>dilute</strong> a signal concentrated in the least-redacted nucleus. It was therefore re-tested over <strong>Genesis 1 (verses 1–31)</strong> —the oldest and least manipulated composition of the corpus— with a Markov null <strong>matched by the real length</strong> of those verses (<code>palindrome.mjs</code>):</p>
<table><thead><tr><th>set</th><th>mirror-palindrome (k=1)</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Genesis, full corpus (n=1533)</td><td>39.0 %</td></tr><tr><td>Markov ord-1 matched by length of Gen 1 (n=40 000)</td><td>38.3 %</td></tr><tr><td>Corpus rate at 4 digits (n=1496)</td><td>39.7 %</td></tr><tr><td><strong>Genesis 1, original nucleus (n=31)</strong></td><td><strong>61.3 % (19/31)</strong></td></tr></tbody></table>
<p><strong>Excess: 1.6× the length-matched null; upper-tail binomial p-value ≈ 8×10⁻³.</strong> It is not an artifact of length or of digit count: the 31 verses of Genesis 1 are almost all 4-digit, and the corpus rate at 4 digits is 39.7 % — the same as the null. The signal is not in the length; it is in the <strong>nucleus</strong>. The corpus-level test (§13) <strong>diluted</strong> it by averaging with the remaining 1502 verses (largely genealogies and later narrative).</p>
<p><strong>Mandatory caveats.</strong> (i) n = 31 is a single chapter. (ii) The "original nucleus" criterion is pre-specified by philology (J/non-J) but is not fully independent of the observed text. (iii) The mirror-palindrome remains arithmetically "easy" (40 % base at 4 digits), so an excess may reflect <strong>deliberate composition of short verses</strong> rather than <strong>astronomical encoding</strong>. (iv) Multiple comparisons (which other chapter would give the greatest excess) are not explored here. For all these reasons, this is a <strong>hypothesis with weak-to-moderate empirical support, not a proof</strong>: the original nucleus is <em>consistently</em> more palindromic than expected, but the mechanism (verse design vs. celestial encoding) remains open.</p>
<blockquote><strong>Integrated reading of §13.</strong> At the corpus level, the mirror does not discriminate (§13.1–13.2); the selective engine is the positional rule <em>S</em> ⊆ <em>O</em> (exponential rarefaction P = q^|S|). At the <strong>original-nucleus</strong> level, the mirror shows a real excess (§13.3). Both results are compatible: the <em>operational</em> selectivity of the <em>Reader of the Sky</em> is positional; the <em>compositional intentionality</em> of the sacred text may leave a trace in the least-redacted nucleus.</blockquote>

<h2 id="14-resultado-iv-el-144">14. Result IV — The 144</h2>
<ol><li><strong>144 = 12²</strong> — the 12 simples squared; the square of the completeness of the zodiac.</li><li><strong>144 = lunar months of the 12 common years of the Metonic cycle:</strong> 12×12 + 7×13 = 144 + 91 = 235 (§7). 144 is structural in lunar–solar synchrony.</li><li><strong>144 = Egel + Ayil = 103 + 41</strong> (§6.2): the gematria of the calf (ending Era of Taurus) plus that of the ram (beginning Era of Aries) sums to 144 —the zodiacal transition in a single figure.</li><li><strong>144 000 = 144 × 1000 = 360 × 400.</strong> Here 360 = the complete zodiacal circle (12×30°) and 400 = ת (Tav), the seventh double, assigned to the <strong>Moon</strong> (§5). 144 000/360 = 400. In the SY framework, "the whole circle × the Moon" = 144 000. (Rev 7/14: 144 000 = 12 tribes × 12 000 = 12² × 1000.)</li><li><strong>144 years = 2.01° of precession</strong> (§3): two degrees of the great precessional clock.</li><li><strong>144 as a divisor of the era and the great year —only at the Platonic rate of 72 y/°—:</strong> 144 × 15 = <strong>2160</strong> (zodiacal era at 72 y/°) and 144 × 180 = <strong>25 920</strong> (great year at 72 y/°). <strong>Caveat:</strong> at the real IAU rate (50.29″/year) the era is 2147.5 y and the great year 25 771 y, and <strong>neither is divisible by 144</strong> (2147.5/144 = 14.913; 25 771/144 = 178.965). The clean divisibility is a property of the 72 y/° rounding, not of the observed precession.</li></ol>
<blockquote>144 is not an isolated figure: it unites the 12 of the zodiac (12²), the 144 lunar months of Meton, the Egel+Ayil transition, the 144 000 = circle×Moon (ת) of apocalyptic symbolism, and —at the Platonic rate— the division of the era (2160) and of the great year (25 920). At the observed rate (50.29″/year) it retains only the 2.01° per 144 years.</blockquote>
<h2 id="15-discusión">15. Discussion</h2>
<p><strong>Two distinct cycles that common sense confuses:</strong></p>
<ul><li><strong>~491 years</strong> (Neptune–Pluto synodic, Aries–Aquarius phase): periodicity <em>of the Genesis legibility window</em> and, empirically, of the religious-linguistic re-formations (§12).</li><li><strong>~2148 years</strong> (precession per sign): periodicity <em>of the background zodiacal Era</em> (§3). The "2000-year intuition" corresponds to this; but <em>Genesis legibility</em> does not wait 2000 years between windows, but ~491.</li></ul>
<p><strong>Genesis 1:1 as an era-marker-verse.</strong> The correlation of the six windows with religious-linguistic re-formations (Axial, Temple, Justinian, Schism, Reformation, present) is an empirical pattern, not a causal demonstration (n = 6). But the recurrence is physically explicable (celestial mechanics, not an <em>ad hoc</em> fit): Genesis 1:1 demands <strong>Aquarius</strong> (צ, incoming era) and <strong>Aries</strong> (טלה, preceding era), anchored by the two slowest planets.</p>
<p><strong>On the discard.</strong> "Why Genesis and not another combination?" — structural answer: the discard is <strong>positional</strong> (<em>S</em> ⊆ <em>O</em>). Genesis was not chosen for an arithmetic seal (§13 rules it out, §9.2 rules out 37/73 in eclipses), but because <strong>its list of simples coincides with the set of signs that the era activates</strong>: Aquarius (צ) demands Pluto; Aries (טלה) demands Neptune.</p>
<p><strong>On the 19.</strong> The 19 unites Meton, Saros, and the basmala (§8): it is the number of lunar synchrony. 144 (§14) is the number of the completeness of 12 applied to the moon (144 months of Meton) and to the circle (144 000 = 360×400). 72 is the precessional degree (§3) and the Name of 72 letters.</p>
<h2 id="15b-cuadrados-mágicos-sigilos-ángeles-y-cierre-de-asignaturas-v3-1">15b. Magic squares, sigils, angels, and closing of outstanding matters (v3.1)</h2>
